DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Rome: Rome Prize Fellowship 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:The Rome Prize supports roughly 30 artists and scholars a year 
 with a residential fellowship at the American Academy in Rome\; discipline
 s include Design and Visual Arts\, where media and new-genre work is regul
 arly funded. Fellows receive a USD 16\,000 (half-term) or USD 30\,000 (ful
 l-term) stipend plus housing\, workspace and weekday meals on the Academy'
 s Janiculum campus. ELIGIBILITY: US citizens for most categories\; foreign
  nationals who have lived in the US for the three years preceding the dead
 line may apply in Environmental Arts and Humanities and certain postdoctor
 al categories. FEES: USD 50 (one category) or USD 60 (multiple) by 1 Novem
 ber 2026\; a late window runs to 15 November at USD 80/90. DEADLINE: 1 Nov
 ember 2026.\n\nOrganisation: American Academy in Rome\nLocation: Rome\, It
 aly (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisation with NYC offi
 ce). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreign nationals resid
 ent in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may apply only in cer
 tain categories.\nAward: Stipends of USD 16\,000 (half-term\, about 5 mont
 hs) and USD 30\,000 (full-term\, about 10 months)\, plus housing\, workspa
 ce and weekday meals. Approximately 30 fellowships per year. APPLICATION F
 EE: USD 50 by 1 November (USD 60 for multiple categories)\; USD 80/90 in t
 he late window to 15 November.\nDuration: 5 or 10 months\n\nMore: https://
 www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rome\, Italy (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisat
 ion with NYC office). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreig
 n nationals resident in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may 
 apply only in certain categories.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:van-alen-re-paris-prize-2026-us-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T154134Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Van Alen Institute: Re:Paris Prize\, USD 35\,000 travel r
 esearch fellowship on design in Africa and its diaspora (US-based applican
 ts)
DESCRIPTION:The Re:Paris Prize\, run by Van Alen Institute\, funds research
  into how design plays a transformative role in Africa and its diaspora. E
 ach winner receives a USD 35\,000 travel fellowship for field research tha
 t requires international travel to connect with experts and opportunities.
  Two Africa-based winners were chosen from the 2026 Pan-African Biennale\;
  a third\, US-based winner is selected through this open call. Proposals a
 ddress one of five themes\, including 'Data\, algorithms\, and the public 
 realm'\, on how digital infrastructures reshape public space\, civic life 
 and spatial perception. Winners present their learnings at Van Alen Instit
 ute in Fall 2027 and at the second Pan-African Biennale in 2028. ELIGIBILI
 TY: US-based applicants\; further rules on the call page. APPLY via the Ai
 rtable form linked from the project page. DEADLINE: Sunday 22 November 202
 6.\n\nOrganisation: Van Alen Institute\nLocation: US-based applicants\; in
 ternational field research travel\, with presentations at Van Alen Institu
 te (New York) in Fall 2027 and the second Pan-African Biennale in 2028.\nA
 ward: USD 35\,000 travel fellowship\; one US-based winner selected through
  this open call (two Africa-based winners were selected via the 2026 Pan-A
 frican Biennale).\nDuration: Research travel\, with presentations in Fall 
 2027 and 2028\n\nMore: https://www.vanalen.org/project/re-paris-prize/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.vanalen.org/project/re-paris-prize/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:US-based applicants\; international field research travel\, with p
 resentations at Van Alen Institute (New York) in Fall 2027 and the second 
 Pan-African Biennale in 2028.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
